! MCP INITIALIZATION, printed p.57 (MCP_Mar63_001-249 PDF p.64) --
! THE IOREQ SEARCH AND SORT.
!
! Thirty-eight lines and ALL THIRTY-EIGHT COMPILE.  No comment rows,
! no heading box: the page is solid code from 003206.00 to 003237.00.
!
! >>> AND IT RUNS STRAIGHT INTO printed p.58. <<<  Line 38 is
! "B,L NORM" at 003237.00, one half word, compiling 003237.50 00 --
! and 003237.40 is printed p.58 line 5.  The two pages are
! contiguous to the bit, and p.58's own last line is pinned by p.59's
! "SLC,$" the same way.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Two nested loops over the IOREQ table and then the same tail
! printed p.58 uses.
!
!   lines 1-10   an RLCT search: load a byte, compare, step down,
!                and "-ACC LOW-- SWITCH RLCT" at line 5.
!   lines 11-30  the IOREQ search and sort proper, with L SEARD /
!                L SEARF / L SEARE / L SEARG as its labels and
!                line 22's "SWAPI,1,0.0(L WORKX),0.0(L IODX)
!                -SWAP IOREQ SLOTS." as the sort's exchange.
!   lines 31-38  the finish: restore L XNT, set the LPPEN bit, step
!                the PPREF index, and return through L NORM.
!
! >>> THE LAST SEVEN LINES ARE printed p.58's ERROR TAIL, TO THE
! BIT. <<<  Compare the two pages' binaries:
!
!     p.57 line 32  000000.47 84  001000.00 F0   = p.58 line 31
!     p.57 line 33  002613.11 10                 = p.58 line 33
!     p.57 line 34  000002.11 07                 = p.58 line 34
!     p.57 line 35  000000.47 84  001000.36 F0   = p.58 line 35
!     p.57 line 37  002720.00 80  000024.06 E0   = p.58 line 38
!
! and p.57 line 36 differs from p.58 line 37 only in its branch
! target (L NORM against L ERR4).  So the normal path and the error
! path do the SAME housekeeping and differ in where they go, which
! is what makes p.58's "L ERR4" rejoin make sense.
!
! >>> AND THIS PAGE IS WHERE printed p.58's T LPPEN dds COMES FROM.
! <<<  Line 32 is "L FIN3  CM0000(BU,1),T LPPEN(L XPP)" -- the dds
! WRITTEN OUT -- and p.58 line 31 is "CM0000,T LPPEN(L XPP)" with
! nothing written.  Both compile 000000.47 84  001000.00 F0.  That
! pair, one page apart, is the evidence that T LPPEN carries
! SYN(BU,1); see decks/mcp_bootstrap_p58.strap's header.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THIS PAGE CONFIRMS FROM printed p.58, INDEPENDENTLY
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! p.58 derived five symbols that no earlier deck had.  Three of them
! appear here too, and the values agree:
!
!   T IOREQ  (8)3373.0   line 14's "LVI,L IODX,T IOREQ" is
!                        003373.07 01, and line 25's
!                        "LVI,L WORKX,T IOREQ" is 003373.25 01 --
!                        THE SAME WORD as p.58 line 21.
!   T LAST   0.18        lines 13 and 24, both ".22" = 0o22 = 18.
!   LASTPP   (8)2613.0   line 33, the same row as p.58 line 33.
!
! Two pages derived them from two different sets of rows and got the
! same answers, which is worth more than either page alone.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! "B0" IS LVE, AND THE MEMORY SAID SO BEFORE THE PAGE WAS OPENED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 6 is "LVE,L XNT,$-1." compiling 003211.23 B0.  B and 8 are
! the only pair in 0-9A-F that differ mainly in one vertical stroke,
! and that stroke is the first thing a worn drum printer loses
! (listing_typography.md 11) -- printed p.3 line 10 was read as 80 at
! 900 dpi and is B0.  Decoding first and looking second: LVE is 11011
! at bits 23-27, so the byte HAD to be B0.  Here it reads B0 cleanly
! at 900 dpi and the operand confirms it from the other side: line 6
! stands at 003212.00, so "$-1." is 003211.0, which is the address
! printed.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! A LEADING "$" ON AN OPERATION, FOR THE SECOND TIME
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 5 prints "$L(BU,8),-0.8(L IODX),46" and is written here as
! "L(BU,8),-0.8(L IODX),46".  printed p.43 line 6 prints
! "$B,Q GO$A" and decks/mcp_bootstrap_p43.strap note (3) says of it:
! "the '$' on the operation is unexplained, and the compiled row is
! checked either way".  That is still true, and this is now TWO
! instances rather than one -- which makes it a listing habit rather
! than a one-off smudge.  Neither row's bits depend on it.
!
! A NEGATIVE BIT ADDRESS, and the listing prints it as one.  Line
! 5's operand is "-0.8(L IODX)" and the compiled address field is
! 777777.70 -- eighteen octal digits of word and 0o70 of bit, which
! as one 24-bit quantity is 0o77777770 = -8.  The row steps the
! search DOWN one byte, which is what "-ACC LOW-- SWITCH RLCT" says.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! ONE SYMBOL POINTS BACKWARD OFF THE PAGE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 30 is "CB,L WORKX,L SEARA" compiling 003205.24 48, so
! L SEARA is 003205.00 -- one word BEFORE this page starts, on
! printed p.56, which is not transcribed yet.  It is a stand-in here
! and p.56 will place it.
!
! TWO LISTING MARKS, the bare "*" after the location: lines 7
! ("003212.40 *") and 24 ("003225.40 *").
!
! ONE LISTING TYPO, in a comment and therefore in no bits: line 28's
! comment reads "-IF NOT OVERLAP MOAD" where lines 16 and 27 say
! MODE.  Transcribed as printed.

        SLC, (8)3206.0

! ---- index registers ----------------------------------------------
LIODX   SYN, $3
LXPP    SYN, $4
LXNT    SYN, $9
LWORKX  SYN, $10
! ---- confirmed from printed p.58 ----------------------------------
TIOREQ  SYN, (8)3373.0
TLAST   SYN(BU,1), 0.18
LASTPP  SYN, (8)2613.0
TLPPEN  SYN(BU,1), 0.39
LOVBIT  SYN(BU,1), (8)2601.62
LNOSAV  SYN, (8)2720.0
LNORM   SYN, (8)3237.40
! ---- new on this page ---------------------------------------------
LRLCT   SYN, (8)2607.0
LCT     SYN, (8)2614.0
LPUT    SYN, (8)2605.0
LSEARA  SYN, (8)3205.0
TUIORQ  SYN, (8)3514.0

        SLC, (8)3206.0

! ---- the RLCT search ----------------------------------------------
        LVI, LXNT, LRLCT             ! line 1
        L(V+I)(BU,8), 0.8(LIODX), 46 ! line 2  -ENTER FIRST RLCT.
LSEARB  KF(V+I)(BU,8), 0.8(LIODX), 46 ! line 3 -INNER LOOP----COMPARE.
        BZALZ, LSEARC                ! line 4  -ACC. NOT LOW----STEP
                                      !           DOWN.
        L(BU,8), -0.8(LIODX), 46     ! line 5  -ACC LOW-- SWITCH RLCT
                                      !   listing prints "$L(BU,8)..."
        LVE, LXNT, $-1.              ! line 6  -PUT PROPER ADDRESS IN
                                      !           XC VF.
LSEARC  CB, LIODX, LSEARB            ! line 7  -LOOP BACK ON NON ZERO
                                      !           CF.
        LC, LIODX, $R                ! line 8  -LOAD XB CF.
        CM0000(BU,8), 0.0(LXNT), 0.0 ! line 9  -ZERO PROPER RLCT SLOT.
        V-I, LXNT, LRLCT             ! line 10 -READY XC FOR RLSYM
                                      !           SEARCH.

! ---- the IOREQ search and sort ------------------------------------
        LV, LIODX, LWORKX            ! line 11 -LOAD XB VF.
        L(BU,8), LCT(LXNT), 0.0      ! line 12 -LOAD HIGH RLSYM.
LSEARD  BZB, TLAST(LIODX), LSEARF    ! line 13 -IS THIS END OF TABLE
        LVI, LIODX, TIOREQ           ! line 14 -  YES ... INITIALIZE
        V+I, $15, 0.0                ! line 15 -TO TEST FOR NOT
                                      !           OVERLAP MODE
        BXCZ, LSEARF                 ! line 16 -OVERLAP MODE
        LVI, LIODX, TUIORQ           ! line 17 -IF NOT OVERLAP MODE
LSEARF  KF(BU,7), .11(LIODX)         ! line 18 -  NO....INNER SEARCH
                                      !           LOOP.
        BAEZ, LSEARE                 ! line 19 -FOUND----STEP DOWN.
        V+I, LIODX, 1.0              ! line 20 -NOT FOUND----STEP XB
                                      !           VF.
        B, LSEARD                    ! line 21 -GO BACK AND TRY AGAIN.
LSEARE  SWAPI, 1, 0.0(LWORKX), 0.0(LIODX)  ! line 22 -SWAP IOREQ
                                      !           SLOTS.
        V+I, LWORKX, 1.0             ! line 23 -STEP XA VF.
        BZB, TLAST(LWORKX), LSEARG   ! line 24 -IS THIS END OF IOREQ
                                      !           TABLE
        LVI, LWORKX, TIOREQ          ! line 25 -YES...INITIALIZE
        V+I, $15, 0.0                ! line 26 -CHECK MODE
        BXCZ, LSEARG                 ! line 27 -IF OVERLAP
        LVI, LWORKX, TUIORQ          ! line 28 -IF NOT OVERLAP MOAD
LSEARG  CB+, LIODX, LSEARD           ! line 29 -  LOOP BACK ON
                                      !           NON-ZERO CF.
        CB, LWORKX, LSEARA           ! line 30 -END OF SWAP AND SORT.

! ---- the finish, which printed p.58 repeats ------------------------
LSKIP   LX, LXNT, LPUT               ! line 31 -RESTORE LXNT INDEX.
LFIN3   CM0000(BU,1), TLPPEN(LXPP)   ! line 32
        SX, LXPP, LASTPP             ! line 33 -SAVE ADR. OF LAST PP
                                      !           ENTERED
        V+ICR, LXPP, 2.0             ! line 34 -STEP PPREF INDEX.
        CM1111(BU,1), TLPPEN(LXPP)   ! line 35 -TURN ON LPPEN BIT
        BZBZ, LOVBIT, LNORM          ! line 36 -IF OVERLAP MODE
        SWAPI, 3, LNOSAV, LXPP       ! line 37 -RESET INDEXES TO
                                      !           OVERLAP MODE
        B, LNORM                     ! line 38 -NORMAL RETURN.
        END, LSEARB

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE CHECKED ROWS -- all thirty-eight.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   line  1  003206.00  002607.23 01                 LVI
!   line  2  003206.40  000000.10 83  110027.20 50   L(V+I)
!   line  3  003207.40  000000.10 83  110027.23 10   L SEARB KF(V+I)
!   line  4  003210.40  003212.76 44                 BZALZ
!   line  5  003211.00  777777.70 83  010027.20 50   L(BU,8),-0.8
!   line  6  003212.00  003211.23 B0                 LVE
!   line  7  003212.40  003207.46 48                 L SEARC CB
!   line  8  003213.00  000011.06 50                 LC
!   line  9  003213.40  000000.00 89  010000.00 F0   CM0000
!   line 10  003214.40  002607.23 0D                 V-I
!   line 11  003215.00  000032.06 30                 LV
!   line 12  003215.40  002614.00 89  010000.20 50   L(BU,8),L CT
!   line 13  003216.40  000000.22 83  003221.74 00   L SEARD BZB
!   line 14  003217.40  003373.07 01                 LVI
!   line 15  003220.00  000000.37 05                 V+I
!   line 16  003220.40  003221.70 42                 BXCZ
!   line 17  003221.00  003514.07 01                 LVI
!   line 18  003221.40  000000.13 83  007000.23 10   L SEARF KF(BU,7)
!   line 19  003222.40  003224.36 C6                 BAEZ
!   line 20  003223.00  000001.07 05                 V+I
!   line 21  003223.40  003216.50 00                 B,L SEARD
!   line 22  003224.00  000000.00 8A  000000.02 E3   L SEARE SWAPI,1
!   line 23  003225.00  000001.25 05                 V+I
!   line 24  003225.40  000000.22 8A  003230.74 00   BZB
!   line 25  003226.40  003373.25 01                 LVI
!   line 26  003227.00  000000.37 05                 V+I
!   line 27  003227.40  003230.70 42                 BXCZ
!   line 28  003230.00  003514.25 01                 LVI
!   line 29  003230.40  003216.47 48                 L SEARG CB+
!   line 30  003231.00  003205.24 48                 CB,L SEARA
!   line 31  003231.40  002605.22 10                 L SKIP  LX
!   line 32  003232.00  000000.47 84  001000.00 F0   L FIN3  CM0000
!   line 33  003233.00  002613.11 10                 SX
!   line 34  003233.40  000002.11 07                 V+ICR
!   line 35  003234.00  000000.47 84  001000.36 F0   CM1111
!   line 36  003235.00  002601.62 80  003237.74 04   BZBZ
!   line 37  003236.00  002720.00 80  000024.06 E0   SWAPI,3
!   line 38  003237.00  003237.50 00                 B,L NORM
